Orcus APK Emulator
==================

This program does not include or redistribute any part of the Android SDK. The Android Emulator,
platform-tools and the system image are downloaded on each PC after a person accepts the Android
Software Development Kit License Agreement (android-sdk-license, section 3.4 forbids redistribution).
The ARM translation in Google system images is licensed for development and debugging only.

The installed program carries these third-party components. Their license texts are in the
licenses folder next to OrcusAPK.exe.

- Python 3.14 runtime - PSF License Agreement, with the licenses of the libraries it bundles
  (OpenSSL, libffi, bzip2, zstd and others): licenses/Python-LICENSE.txt
- PySide6-Essentials / shiboken6 6.12.0 (Qt for Python and the Qt 6 libraries) - LGPL-3.0:
  licenses/LGPL-3.0.txt and licenses/GPL-3.0.txt (the LGPL-3.0 adds its permissions to the GPL-3.0).
  The Qt libraries are separate, replaceable DLLs in _internal/PySide6/ (Qt6Core.dll, Qt6Gui.dll,
  Qt6Widgets.dll, Qt6Network.dll and the plugins); you may replace them with your own builds of the
  same Qt version. Their source code: https://download.qt.io/official_releases/qt/ (Qt) and
  https://download.qt.io/official_releases/QtForPython/ (PySide6, shiboken6).
- grpcio 1.85.0 - Apache-2.0, with its third-party notices: licenses/grpcio-LICENSE
- protobuf 7.36.2 - BSD-3-Clause: licenses/protobuf-LICENSE
- apkInspector 1.3.7 - Apache-2.0: licenses/apkinspector-LICENSE
- typing_extensions 4.16.0 - PSF-2.0: licenses/typing_extensions-LICENSE
- PyInstaller 6.22.3 bootloader (the two EXEs) - GPL-2.0 with the bootloader exception, which allows
  distributing programs built with it under any terms: licenses/pyinstaller-COPYING.txt

Vendored files:

- Android Emulator gRPC .proto files (emulator build 16428233) - Apache-2.0,
  Copyright The Android Open Source Project. Kept in src/orcus/emugrpc/protos/<build>/ with their headers;
  the Python stubs generated from them are part of the program.

The program is not code-signed: Windows SmartScreen may warn the first time the installer runs.
